  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Wisconsin totaled $3.4B in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 56,531 awards with an average award size of $59.8K, and obligations fell 46.0% year over year. Current-year totals are partial because these figures are fiscal year to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying activity with $2.1B in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $826M. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. was the top vendor with $1.9B in obligations. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) was the largest industry sector with $1.8B in obligations. These totals reflect where federal dollars were obligated in Wisconsin through the reporting period, and they show concentration in health services, vehicle and heavy equipment manufacturing, and medical-related industries.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Wisconsin changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 46.0% year over year. Total obligations reached $3.4B in FY2026 to date compared with prior fiscal years where obligations ranged from $5.2B to $8.9B. Award activity remains robust with 56,531 awards and an average award size of $59.8K, but the fiscal year to date total is partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $2.1B. The Department of Defense obligated $826M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $182M. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. is the largest vendor with $1.9B, followed by OSHKOSH DEFENSE LLC with $738M and AMTEC CORPORATION with $267M."
      }
    ]
  },
